        "content": "<p>alexcrichton opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15265\">PR #15265</a> from <code>alexcrichton:remove-shared-everything-threads</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This commit removes the current flags/gates Wasmtime has for the shared-everything-threads proposal. There hasn't been activity here in quite some time and Wasmtime can trivially panic on many inputs using shared-everything-threads, so remove it for now so it all fails in validation rather than getting further within Wasmtime.</p>\n<p>&lt;!--<br>\nPlease make sure you include the following information:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>If this work has been discussed elsewhere, please include a link to that<br>\n  conversation. If it was discussed in an issue, just mention \"issue #...\".</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Explain why this change is needed. If the details are in an issue already,<br>\n  this can be brief.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Our development process is documented in the Wasmtime book:<br>\n<a href=\"https://docs.wasmtime.dev/contributing-development-process.html\">https://docs.wasmtime.dev/contributing-development-process.html</a></p>\n<p>Please review the Bytecode Alliance's AI tool usage policy at<br>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/governance/blob/main/AI_TOOL_POLICY.md\">https://github.com/bytecodealliance/governance/blob/main/AI_TOOL_POLICY.md</a></p>\n<p>Please ensure all communication follows the code of conduct:<br>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a><br>\n--&gt;</p>\n</blockquote>",
